From 30f9fea804f7dfe35d69855797490f7e4334d570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 03:16:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08039/11362] The change gate catches both named vacuous
 engines and spares the good one -- at a call site the lp85 acceptance never
 reached

PHASE 4, measurement only. No default flipped, no threshold lowered.
SUBMITTED_WORLD_MODEL_CHANGE_GATE_ENABLED is still False.

Nine engines, byte-exact from the 2026-07-30 force-admit audit (every staged file's
sha256[:16] equals that cell's recorded src_engine_sha256; tn36-on additionally equals
the frozen Phase-3 fixture). Graded on the captured corpora, whose identity is CHECKED
rather than assumed -- 8 of 8 audit fields reproduce exactly on all 8 cells that have
them, and sc25-on is excluded with its reason attached because its audit record is all
nulls (terminal induce ended proposer_failed_or_missing_root).

Both pre-registered targets are caught for DISCRIMINATING reasons, and the good engine
passes. The admission swap adds ZERO new admits against either incumbent configuration:
under the shipped exact>=0.5 it removes lp85-on (acc 0.920, 96 invented cells); under
CARNOT_ARC_TRUST_METRIC=cell_recall it removes ft09-onb (cell_recall 0.947, a
hallucinated change on 19 of 19 no-ops); tn36-on is retained by both.

Four things the flattering half of that result hides, all recorded in scope_limits.

The flag does not govern the site the diagnosis points at. change_gate_decision is
called ZERO times in arc_llm_reinduction.py; that module admits on heldout_accuracy
alone. "lp85 rounds 2-3 scored heldout 1.0 and were ACCEPTED" describes THAT admission,
so flipping the flag would not have changed those rounds' fate.

It is also not those rounds' engine. Retention kept round 1, and that is what carries
the 96 invented cells -- confirmed by reproducing the audit's 0.92 / 0.4369 / 96
exactly. Rounds 2 and 3 were never retained and are unrecoverable, so what the gate
would do to them is unmeasured and unclaimed.

The catch mechanism is not the one the framing implies. n_changes_correct 0 is
TRANSITION-level; the gate's non-degeneracy floor is the CELL-level
correct_changed_cells, which is 256, so that branch never fires. lp85 is caught by
change_fidelity 0.375 < 0.5 -- a 0.125 margin over an n_changing of 2.

And the must-not-fire side is n=1, because the run produced exactly one sound engine.
Two priors bear on it and DISAGREE: exp6011 rejects the hand-written dc22 control
mask-off 3/3 and says do not flip without the mask; exp6013 admits the same control
mask-off 3/3 through the production path. Unresolved, and not resolved here.

Predicted funnel effect: none. Neither newly-rejected engine was reaching the policy,
and vc33 -- the one cell that did -- has every change-gate field null, so its engine
never arrived at this call site. This is a precision change, not a funnel change.

Recommendation: qualified yes, not acted on. Settling it needs a must-not-fire
population larger than one and a resolution of exp6011-vs-exp6013 first.

